From a3278dc692e0f7a6069ef1c79e15977216f35f0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arc-moe <arc-moe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 07:18:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] sycl: kernels launch as ordinary kernels on Alchemist (no
 use_root_sync)

dpct gave all 318 kernel launches sycl::ext::oneapi::experimental::
use_root_sync, which makes DPC++ submit them as cooperative kernels
(zeCommandListAppendLaunchCooperativeKernel). No kernel uses a root-group
barrier, so the property buys only the cooperative path's constraints. On
2x Arc A770 (i915) the first kernel launched on the second GPU of the layer
split - gather_rows in MtpDrafter::bind, 384 x 256 - fails with
UR_RESULT_ERROR_OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY right after a clean wait on that device.

The property is now the macro STRATA_ROOT_SYNC_PROP, empty when
STRATA_SYCL_NO_ROOT_SYNC (ON by default for Alchemist targets): the same
kernels, launched the ordinary way. Battlemage builds keep the property.
